---
import CoverageGrid from "../CoverageGrid.astro";
import { unseen } from "../../lib/coverage";

const report = [
  { key: "rosters", text: "Rosters were collected for all seven schools.", answer: "strike", why: `Strike. Dunmore's roster is no collector. Rosters are held for ${unseen.rosters} of 7.` },
  { key: "held", text: `No Dunmore page was read for 2025, and the season file still holds ${unseen.dunmoreHeld} Dunmore matches.`, answer: "keep", why: `Keep. All ${unseen.dunmoreHeld} came from opponents' pages, and the sentence says how many are held without claiming that is all of them.` },
  { key: "boxes", text: `Box scores are held for ${unseen.withBox} of ${unseen.held} conference matches, so the 2025 season is short of ${unseen.held - unseen.withBox} box scores.`, answer: "strike", why: `Strike. The first half is true of the file. The second half is a claim about the season, which holds ${unseen.expected} matches, so as many as ${unseen.expected - unseen.withBox} are without a box score. A denominator taken from the run cannot show what the run missed.` },
  { key: "why", text: "Eastbrook State's own box-score pages could not be listed, because its schedule could not be proved.", answer: "keep", why: "Keep. The record gives exactly that reason, and the sentence claims nothing about the matches themselves." },
  { key: "zero", text: "Dunmore's site returned no conference matches for 2025.", answer: "strike", why: "Strike. Nothing was returned because nothing could be read, which is a different fact from “none.”" },
];
---

<section id="prove-it">
  <h2>Prove it: the season nobody called about</h2>
  <p>This is the sample's real coverage record for the season before: Prairie Lakes men, 2025. Hartwell Tech had not joined, and the format was the same. Conference matches are missing from this season too, and no coach phoned about them.</p>
  <p>On Friday, Riley's readers were the monitoring. A coverage record does that job before anyone publishes. Tap the squares that are not complete and read each reason.</p>
  <CoverageGrid rows={unseen.grid} caption="Coverage record, Prairie Lakes men, 2025" id="past" />

  <h4 class="cv-try">Red-pen the report</h4>
  <p>The season file holds {unseen.held} conference matches, and box scores for {unseen.withBox} of them. Kick wrote five sentences about the season. Answer the question first, then keep each sentence the record supports and strike the rest.</p>
  <div class="cv-check" data-once="report">
    <div data-q data-type="number" data-answer={unseen.expected} data-why={`${unseen.expected}. Seven schools each host the other six: 7 × 6, from the membership list and the format.`}>
      <label for="cv-expected">How many conference matches should the 2025 season hold?</label>
      <input id="cv-expected" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" data-save="q-expected" />
      <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    {report.map((r) => (
      <fieldset class="cv-line" data-q data-type="radio" data-answer={r.answer} data-why={r.why}>
        <legend>“{r.text}”</legend>
        <label><input type="radio" name={`rep-${r.key}`} value="keep" data-save={`rep-${r.key}`} /><span>Keep</span></label>
        <label><input type="radio" name={`rep-${r.key}`} value="strike" data-save={`rep-${r.key}`} /><span>Strike</span></label>
        <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
      </fieldset>
    ))}
    <p class="cv-once">One attempt at all six.</p>
    <button type="button" data-submit>Check my marks</button>
    <p class="cv-fb" role="status" data-need></p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <p>Three counts describe this season, and all three are true: {unseen.schedules} of 7 schedules, {unseen.held} of {unseen.expected} matches, and box scores for {unseen.withBox} of {unseen.expected}. Each counts a different unit. “{unseen.withBox} of {unseen.held}” is true of the file, and becomes false when someone reads it as the season. A count taken from the run belongs only beside the count against the expected set, with the gaps named.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cv-commit" data-commit>
    <label class="cv-write" for="cv-caption">Now write the line that goes under the 2025 conference table when it is published.</label>
    <textarea id="cv-caption" rows="3" data-save="caption"></textarea>
    <button type="button" disabled>Compare with a worked answer</button>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write a full sentence to compare.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <p class="cv-model">Built from {unseen.held} of {unseen.expected} conference matches. Not collected: both meetings of Dunmore and Eastbrook State. Each of those two schools has two more scheduled matches than this table shows.</p>
      <fieldset class="cv-ticks">
        <legend>Read your line again and mark it honestly.</legend>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="cap-count" /><span>It gives the count and the total</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="cap-gap" /><span>It names the gap, so a reader can tell which rows to distrust</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="cap-true" /><span>It states nothing about two results nobody has seen</span></label>
      </fieldset>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cv-next">One idea is left: none of this was ever about soccer.</p>
</section>
